{"type":"session","date":"2026-05-22","content":"# Session Notes: 2026-05-22\n\n## Session Overview\n- **Date**: 2026-05-22\n- **Main Topics**: 05BEC Scanning (5 new LPs) + Topic Building (Quarterly Business Review)\n- **New Language Points**: account for, be split into, give an overview of, future opportunities/areas of growth, That brings me to the end of\n- **Progress**: 05BEC scanning completed, 5 new LPs added\n\n---\n\n### 1. 🏋️ 热身 (Archived Review)\n\n**Category**: Archived Gaps Random Check\n\n#### Q1: `could have` in if-clause taboo\n- **Prompt**: \"我当时要是能来参加就好了\"\n- **Student**: `If I could have taken part in it, that would have been great.` ✅\n- **Note**: 正确回避 `could have` 在 if 从句的禁忌。主句 `would have been` 配合精准。\n\n#### Q2: `aware of` preposition\n- **Prompt**: \"你意识到这个问题的严重性了吗？\"\n- **Student**: `Are you aware of the seriousness of this problem?` ✅\n- **Note**: `aware of` 介词固化。\n\n**Result**: 2/2 满分 🏆\n\n---\n\n### 2. ⚡ Flash Correct\n\n#### FC1: Tag Pronoun Matching\n- **Prompt**: \"你的团队已经知道这个消息了，是吗？\"\n- **Student**: `Your team has known this message, hasn't they?` ❌\n  - `hasn't they` → `haven't they` (hasn't 配单数，they 配复数，不匹配)\n- **Correction**: `Your team has known about this, haven't they?`\n  - 同时纠正 `know this message` → `know about this message`\n- **Evaluation**: Tag 代词不匹配仍有余震。`team` 为集合名词，英式用 they 指代时，助动词必须用 haven't。\n\n#### FC2: `know about`\n- **Prompt**: \"这周我没参加会议，但我知道会议的内容。\"\n- **Student**: `I didn't take part in the meeting this week. However, I know about the content of this meeting.` ✅\n  - `didn't take part in` 过去时 ✅\n  - `know about` 正确表示\"知道存在/内容\" ✅\n  - `However` 衔接自然 ✅\n- **Evaluation**: 满分 🏆。`know about` 使用准确。\n\n**FC Result**: 1.5/2 (Tag 代词回退 ⚠️)\n\n---\n\n### 3. 📝 05BEC 未记录语言点训练\n\n#### LP 1: `account for` (占比例)\n\n**概念探询**: 学生表示\"表示占比\" ✅ 核心理解正确。\n\n**Round 1 (肯定陈述)**:\n- **中文**: \"亚太区占了我们总营收的 40%。\"\n- **学生**: `Asia accounts for 40% of our total turnover.` ✅\n- **评价**: 结构标准，`of` 没漏。`turnover` 复用课文词汇亮点 🏆\n\n**Round 2 (否定陈述)**:\n- **中文**: \"自由职业者的收入只占他们总收入的一小部分。\"\n- **学生**: `The revenue of freelancers only accounts for a small part of their total revenue.` ⚠️ 结构正确，但 `revenue of freelancers` 和 `their total revenue` 指向同一概念，逻辑循环\n- **导师建议**: → `Freelance income accounts for only a small part of their total earnings.`\n- **补充辨析**: `revenue` (公司流水) vs `earnings` (个人所得/公司净利润)\n  - 学生对两者无区分意识，讲解后能正确判断\n- **验证题**: \"我们团队的总 _____ 比去年增长了 30%。\"\n  - **学生**: `revenue` ✅ (团队=内部组织，描述流水)\n\n**Round 3 (特殊疑问句)**:\n- **中文**: \"哪个部门占了公司总开支的最大比例？\"\n- **学生**: 未回答（学生转而提问 earnings/revenue 区别）\n- **评价**: 概念辨析自然融入，对 `revenue` vs `earnings` 理解建立。\n\n**Round 4 (反义疑问句)**:\n- **中文**: \"营销部占了总预算的 60%，是吧？\"\n- **学生**: `The marketing department accounts for 60% of the total budget, doesn't it?` ✅ `doesn't it` (department 单数→it)\n- **小问题**: `doesn` 拼写缺撇号，但不影响语法理解。\n\n**Round 5 (Type 3 虚拟语气)**:\n- **中文**: \"如果营销部去年没占到那么高的预算比例，我们就不会有资金问题。\"\n- **学生**: `If the marketing department had not accounted for that huge part of the budget, we would not have had issues with the money.` ✅\n  - `had not accounted for` ✅\n  - `would not have had` ✅\n- **小问题**: `issues with the money` → `funding issues` 或 `budget issues`（更商务）。\n\n**LP 1 状态**: 🏆 **5 句式全通关**\n\n---\n\n#### LP 2: `be split into` (被划分为)\n\n**Round 1 (完成时被动)**:\n- **中文**: \"这个项目被划分成了三个阶段。\"\n- **学生**: `This project has been split into three phases.` ✅ 完成时被动完美 🏆\n\n**Round 2 (否定陈述)**:\n- **中文**: \"这个部门没有分拆成小团队。\"\n- **学生**: `This department isn't split into small teams.` ✅ 一般现在时被动正确 🏆\n\n**Round 3 (特殊疑问句)**:\n- **中文**: \"你们的产品线分成了多少个类别？\"\n- **学生**: `How many categories has your product line split into?` ⚠️\n  - 用了主动语态 `has...split into`。`be split into` 是被动搭配\n- **修正**: → `How many categories is your product line split into?`\n- **重试**: `How many parts is your product line split into?` ✅ 🏆\n\n**Round 4 (反义疑问句)**:\n- **中文**: \"公司分成了四个部门，是吧？\"\n- **学生**: `The company is split into four divisions, isn't it?` ✅ 🏆\n\n**Round 5 (Type 3 虚拟语气被动)**:\n- **中文**: \"如果当时公司没有被分成那么多部门，沟通就会顺畅得多。\"\n- **学生**: `If the company had not had been split into so many divisions, the communication would have been much smoother.` ❌\n  - `had not had been split` → `had not been split` (Type 3 被动过度纠正。公式: had + been + pp，中间不需要第二个 had)\n- **修正**: `If the company had not been split into so many divisions, communication would have been much smoother.`\n\n**LP 2 状态**: 🟡 **Type 3 被动结构需巩固**\n\n---\n\n#### LP 3: `give an overview of` (概述)\n\n**概念探询**: 学生能准确区分 `give an overview of` (事前概览) vs `introduce` (引入主题) vs `summarize` (事后总结)。✅ 🏆\n\n**Round 1 (肯定句)**:\n- **中文**: \"我先简要概述一下这个项目的时间线。\"\n- **学生**: `Let me give an overview of the project timeline.` ✅ 🏆 地道过渡句式\n\n**Round 2 (否定句)**:\n- **中文**: \"他在会议开始时没有概述讨论的要点。\"\n- **学生**: `He didn't give an overview of the main points before the meeting started.` ✅ 否定过去式正确。`before` vs `at the start of` 细微偏差（不影响核心结构）\n\n**Round 3 (Type 3 虚拟语气)**:\n- **中文**: \"如果当时他先概述了项目的范围，团队就不会走错方向了。\"\n- **学生**: `If he had given an overview of the scope of the project, the team would not have gone the wrong way.` ✅\n  - `had given an overview of` ✅\n  - `would not have gone` ✅\n- **小问题**: `gone the wrong way` → `gone in the wrong direction`（介词 `in` 遗漏）\n\n**LP 3 状态**: 🏆 3 句式全通关\n\n---\n\n#### LP 4: `future opportunities / areas of growth` (未来机遇/增长领域)\n\n**Round 1 (肯定句)**:\n- **中文**: \"我们需要识别新兴市场的未来机遇。\"\n- **学生**: `We need to recognize the future opportunities of emerging markets.` ✅ 结构正确\n- **建议**: `recognize` → `identify` (更契合\"发现新机会\"的语境)\n\n**Round 2 (否定/条件句)**:\n- **中文**: \"如果我们不关注增长领域，就会失去市场优势。\"\n- **学生**: `If we don't pay attention to areas of growth, we will lost advantages in market.` ⚠️\n  - `will lost` → `will lose` ❌ 情态动词后原形（旧缺口复发）\n  - `advantages in market` → `competitive edge in the market` 或 `market advantages`（缺冠词 + 搭配调整）\n- **修正**: `If we don't pay attention to areas of growth, we will lose our competitive edge in the market.`\n\n**Round 3 (反义疑问句)**:\n- **中文**: \"这些都是未来重要的增长领域，对吧？\"\n- **学生**: `These are the important areas of growth in the future, aren't they?` ✅\n  - `aren't they` (these→they) ✅\n  - `areas of growth` 短语完整 ✅\n\n**LP 4 状态**: 🟢 (肯定/反义疑问满分；否定句情态动词原形复发 ⚠️)\n\n---\n\n#### LP 5: `That brings me to the end of` (演示结束语)\n\n**语体辨析**:\n- `That brings me to the end of...` — 正式演示收尾\n- `That's all for today` — 中性/偏口语\n- `I'll wrap up here` — 随意\n- **学生判断正确** 🏆\n\n**LP 5 状态**: ✅ 语体理解过关\n\n---\n\n### 4. 🧠 话题构建训练 (Topic Building)\n\n**话题**: 向管理层汇报季度业务进展 (Quarterly Business Review)\n\n**第一步：中文 Brainstorm**\n- 场景：向 VP 和各部门负责人汇报季度成果\n- **学生中文观点**:\n  > \"当前季度我们上了三个游戏，这三个游戏，平均给我们的日活带来了10%的增长。目前这三个游戏的流量占比达到了60%。目前来说，我们最大挑战就是我们上新游戏的速度，每上一个游戏，目前需要花费平均一个月的时间。其中涉及到多个部门之间的沟通。因此我认为我们下个季度的重点就是缩短新游戏的上线时间，同时也不降低游戏的质量。\"\n- **评价**: ✅ 逻辑链清晰：成果 → 数据 → 挑战 → 根因 → 下季度规划\n\n**第二步：骨架供给**\n- **骨架 1** (开场+成果): `This quarter, I'd like to give an overview of our performance. We launched three new games, which together accounted for roughly a 10% increase in our daily active users.`\n- **骨架 2** (数据占比): `Currently, these three games account for about 60% of our total traffic. Our portfolio can now be split into two main parts: the new games and our existing titles.`\n- **骨架 3** (挑战+根因): `That said, our biggest challenge right now is the speed of launching new games. It currently takes about a month per game, largely because the process involves coordination across multiple departments.`\n- **骨架 4** (下季度规划): `So going forward, our key priority for next quarter is to reduce launch time without compromising quality. This is a key area of growth for us, and I see significant future opportunities here.`\n\n**第三步：有脚手架输出**\n- **学生原文**:\n  > `Well, let me give an overview of our performance for this quarter. We have launched three new games and it helped increase 10% of our daily active users. And these three games account for roughly 60% of our total traffic. That said, our biggest challenge here is the speed of launching a new game. Currently it takes about a month per game on average, because it involves collaboration across multiple departments. Going forward, I think our key priority is to reduce the launch time of a new game without compromising game quality and I think this is a key area of growth for us and the future opportunities are significant here.`\n\n**评价**: 骨架全部用上，逻辑连贯 🏆\n\n| 问题 | 原文 | 修正 |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `it helped increase 10% of` | 单数 `it` 不匹配 `three games` | `they helped increase our DAU by 10%` |\n| `and I think... and I think` | 一句话内两次 `and I think` 重复 | 第二个改为 `— which is` |\n\n**第四步：撤脚手架重说**\n- **学生先提出**: \"在使用骨架之前，我想要知道 `that said` 和 `going forward` 这两个词组表达的什么意思。\"\n  - 学生对 `That said` (话虽如此) 和 `Going forward` (展望未来) 先前无概念，但在骨架输出中已用对 ✅\n  - 讲解后理解到位\n- **学生原文**:\n  > `Well, this quarter, we've launched three new games and they brought good performance because they increased our daily user activity by 10%. That said, one of our biggest challenges is the speed of launching a new game because currently it takes us about a month per game on average. So going forward, I think one of our key priorities is to reduce the launch time. And I think this is a significant area of growth for us. And the future opportunities are great here.`\n\n**评价**: 🏆 撤骨架后表达更简洁自然\n\n**改进**:\n| 原文 | 建议 | 问题 |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| `brought good performance` | `delivered solid results` / `performed well` | 中文化表达 |\n| `the future opportunities are great` | `there are significant future opportunities ahead` | `great` 在商务汇报中过于模糊 |\n\n**话题构建总体评价**:\n| 维度 | 评价 |\n|:---|:---|\n| 中文内容质量 | 🏆 逻辑链完整，层层递进 |\n| 骨架使用 | 🏆 全部骨架4个都用上了 |\n| 新LP复用 | 🏆 give an overview of / account for / areas of growth / future opportunities |\n| 撤骨架表现 | ✅ 自然流畅，无重大错误 |\n\n---\n\n### 5. 🔴 不足与待强化 (Improvement Areas)\n\n| # | 缺口 | 类型 | 严重程度 |\n|:---|:---|:---|:---:|\n| 1 | **Tag 代词不匹配** — `hasn't they` (team→they 时助动词应为 haven't) | 旧缺口复发 | 🔴\n| 2 | **情态动词后原形** — `will lost` → `will lose` | 旧缺口复发 | 🔴\n| 3 | **Type 3 被动过度纠正** — `had not had been split` (had + been + pp 即可) | 新发现 | 🔴\n| 4 | **百分比介词遗漏** — `increase 10%` → `increase by 10%` | 新发现 | 🟡\n| 5 | **冠词遗漏 (market)** — `advantages in market` → `advantages in the market` | 旧缺口复发 | 🟡\n| 6 | **方向介词遗漏** — `gone the wrong way` → `gone in the wrong direction` | 新发现 | 🟡\n| 7 | **中文化表达** — `brought good performance` → `delivered solid results` | 新发现 | 🟡\n\n---\n\n### 6. 🛠️ 下次会话行动项\n- [ ] **隔夜抽查**: `account for` (占比), `be split into` (Type 3 被动), `give an overview of` (概述)\n- [ ] **Tag 代词匹配专项**: 集体名词(team/audience/committee)作主语时 Tag 的助动词 + 代词匹配\n- [ ] **情态动词+原形加固**: `will lost` / `cannot came` 等——虽非首次，但今天有复发，需要持续监控\n- [ ] **04BEC 🟡 巩固抽查**（上次遗留: start school / take part in / with + doing）\n"}